Playground core: keep request bodies when the browser cannot stream them (Firefox)

Firefox does not expose Request.body and sends a ReadableStream request body as
the text "[object ReadableStream]", yet it passes Playground's streaming probe.
So a CORS-proxy retry from fetchWithCorsProxy() went out without its body, and
so did a PHP request (curl or wp_remote_post) carried over the TCP-over-fetch
bridge. This patch fixes the probe, reads the retry body with arrayBuffer() when
the clone exposes no stream, and buffers the bridged body before the fetch.

The deploy workflow (.github/workflows/deploy-site.yml, playground-build job)
applies this file with `git apply` to the WordPress Playground release it builds.
Record and upstream draft: docs/changes/2026-11-20-playground-core-request-body-firefox.md.
Remove it once the pinned Playground release contains the fix; the build fails
if it no longer applies.

